Robot infos1
ROBOT: 4-legged crawler, 8 servos, 2 DOF per leg, no knee (final design).

TORSO: square. One leg at each corner, on the 45° diagonal.
Front = top of the top-view sketch.

SERVO LABELS (top view, front at top):
  1 = front-left    2 = front-right
  3 = rear-left     4 = rear-right
Layer 1 (yaw) servos: 1-4. Layer 2 (lift) servos: n+4, so
leg 1 -> servo 5, leg 2 -> 6, leg 3 -> 7, leg 4 -> 8.

LEG (identical x4, each mounted rotated 90° from its neighbors):
- Layer 1 (yaw): vertical axis, swings the limb horizontally.
  Servo range 0-180° via PWM. Commanded 90° = center = limb on the
  corner's 45° diagonal.
  Yaw direction (increasing angle = toward front or rear): [fill in per leg]
- Layer 2 (lift): horizontal hinge axis, perpendicular to the limb.
  Commanded 90° = limb horizontal, pointing outward, parallel to the
  ground. Servos are mirrored:
    at 180°: servos 5 and 8 = limb DOWN, servos 6 and 7 = limb UP.
    So lift direction sign: legs 1 and 4 = one sign, legs 2 and 3 = opposite.
- Foot moves on a fixed-radius arc. Reach cannot be changed.
- No further joints will be added.

GAIT GOALS: crawl gait (one leg lifts at a time, 3 feet always on the
ground), tank-style turning, later IMU + PID tilt correction.
Static stability first, no AI/RL for v1.

CODE CONVENTIONS NEEDED: per-leg sign flip and offset for mirroring,
per-servo trim for calibration, joint limits to prevent leg collisions,
smooth (rate-limited) servo motion, abstract "lift" and "swing" angles
mapped to raw servo angles per leg.

HARDWARE:
- Servos: 8x SG90-class metal-gear micro servos (black plastic case),
  modified/set up for 180° travel. Likely ~2 kg·cm torque at 5-6 V.
- Controller: ESP32. Servo driver: PCA9685 (I2C).
- Sensors: MPU6050 IMU, HMC compass (possibly optional).
  All on one I2C bus (typical addresses: PCA9685 0x40, MPU6050 0x68,
  HMC5883L 0x1E).
- Power: 7.4 V battery -> buck converter -> 5.5 V, feeding both the ESP32
  and the PCA9685 servo rail. Grounds common.
- PCA9685 channel mapping: [confirm, assumed channel = servo label - 1]
- Torso size: TBD
- Limb length: TBD (foot not installed yet, length undecided)
- Total mass: TBD
